      "writtenOn": "2023-10-24T16:54:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`ReadIndexList` will not return HCI if it is currently in use via `HCI_USERCHANNEL`. Can you confirm whether we correctly handle the case of btmanagerd restarting while there are existing btadapterd instances running?",
      "revId": "1f427f154eb0f446a3dc3cc222852d62a4076359",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2e432e08_e0fe8485",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 9,
      "author": {
        "id": 1962300
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-25T07:22:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What\u0027s your expected behavior here?\n\nOn started, btmanagerd lists the PID directory so it\u0027s aware of the running (virtual) index 0, however, the real index doesn\u0027t present until btadaperd is disabled. From btmanagerd\u0027s perspective it couldn\u0027t and shouldn\u0027t map the virtual index to any devpath or real index.\n\nBut Floss actually assumes the real \u003d virtual in this case[1][2][3][4], it\u0027s not quite correct. We probably need to define a way to map the orphan btadapterd to a real index (add more info in pid file name?).\n\n1:https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/gd/rust/linux/mgmt/src/state_machine.rs;l\u003d221;drc\u003d8274613c2709c58ea4016a2e893afd3b8ba2d44e\n2:https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/gd/rust/linux/mgmt/src/state_machine.rs;l\u003d1058;drc\u003d8274613c2709c58ea4016a2e893afd3b8ba2d44e\n3:https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/gd/rust/linux/mgmt/src/state_machine.rs;l\u003d1388;drc\u003d8274613c2709c58ea4016a2e893afd3b8ba2d44e\n4:https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/gd/rust/linux/mgmt/src/state_machine.rs;l\u003d1461;drc\u003d8274613c2709c58ea4016a2e893afd3b8ba2d44e",
      "parentUuid": "b1e130be_3fd61eed",
      "revId": "1f427f154eb0f446a3dc3cc222852d62a4076359",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "84757399_9bf37daa",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 9,
      "author": {
        "id": 1836438
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-25T17:59:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think if you start writing the virtual index and sysfs path to the config file, you can recover from such a scenario.\n\nWe will need to implement a migration for the `btmangagerd.json` file and then store the following per adapter:\n* Sticky Virtual Index\n* Current Real Index\n* Current sysfs path\n\nThe sysfs path is used to identify where the device is plugged in and can be used to disambiguate if we ever have two controllers switch real indicies (which could happen if we support external BT dongles).\n\nThe start-up ordering for btmanagerd would change a bit too:\n* First load up the config and create internal data for virt index mapping.\n* Then ReadIndexList\n* Then apply HciPresense + Pid scanning.",
      "parentUuid": "2e432e08_e0fe8485",
      "revId": "1f427f154eb0f446a3dc3cc222852d62a4076359",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
